# Pi-Star OS graphical-boot sentinel.
#
# This file's EXISTENCE is the signal. It tells Pi-Star MCP and the
# pistar-splash service that this OS has set up for framebuffer output:
# a quiet kernel console (quiet, logo.nologo, no cursor - see make_cmdline
# in bootslot.sh) and a free graphics VT (tty7 carries no getty).
#
# Only then do they take over tty7 and draw the boot logo and the "connect
# here" screen. On an older OS, or native Alpine, this file is absent and
# they stay dormant, leaving the console untouched.
#
# Remove it to keep the console plain and stop the framebuffer takeover.
